Thank you, David.

As I have stated before, this landlord has engaged in nefarious practices
and now clearly criminal actions. In fact, the space my personal property
was moved into is NOT a locker. It is a closet with a single lock. A locker
should be defined as a small lockable closet or compartment, typically as
one of a number placed together and the tenants belongings are ALWAYS
protected by two locks - that of the locker itself and that of the storage
facility. The landlord has attempted to rename the space being used, moved
and potentially damaged my property without my permission, which I
expressly forbade, and the result is less security than I had before.

The measurements of the closet, which does not meet the requirements of
denotation of meaning for 'locker' I will get later.

Please give me information on what forms I require for the filing of the
claim.

Thank you,
Evan Rosner


